{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory met the safety chain: the doctor repeatedly screened biliary red flags, separated emergency thresholds from hepatobiliary outpatient/surgical follow-up, reconstructed the incomplete handoff, and created executable medication and follow-up plans. The doctor actively reprioritized when insulin/food-intake risk and hypoglycemia emerged, and later maintained bounded closure with clear residual risks, written-plan requirements, and caregiver receipt. No serious or minor responsibility-chain error is decisive in the observable trajectory; multiple high-order points were completed with meaningful trajectory impact, supporting a Perfect grade.",
